// The dedicated server `cargo xtask e2e`'s online run joins (`xtask/src/e2e.rs`,
// `fixtures/autoplay/online.ron`): port 0 (the run reads the port from the
// log's "listening on port N"), listed on the run's own Nostr relay
// (`olr-cli nostr-relay --listen 127.0.0.1:0`; xtask replaces `{relay}`
// with its URL) at its public address 127.0.0.1 (`allow_local`, N62), so
// the game finds it on the Internet tab and joins it there, after joining
// it once by the typed address. No STUN server and no port mapping: nothing
// leaves the machine and the real router is never asked. No fill bots, one
// short match on Dirt Level that starts when the game's player and the
// run's bot client (`olr-cli net-client --bot`) are both ready.
(
    name: "e2e server",
    visibility: Public,
    relays: ["{relay}"],
    public_address: Some("127.0.0.1"),
    allow_local: true,
    stun: [],
    port_mapping: false,
    port: 0,
    max_players: 4,
    max_spectators: 2,
    fill_bots: 0,
    rotation: [
        (mod: "olx-classic", level: "olx-level-dirt-level", time_limit: 0.2, kill_limit: 0, lives: -2),
    ],
    start_when_ready: true,
    min_players: 2,
)
